# Every local env file (e.g. .envprod from `vercel env pull`); only the documented template is tracked
.env*
!.env.example

# macOS Finder junk — matches at any depth, no need to gitignore per-folder
.DS_Store

# Internal working docs for Play Console submission prep — draft analysis of
# privacy-policy/data-safety gaps, kept locally for filling out the forms, not
# meant to live in a public repo's history. See store-listing/ for the actual
# (public-facing) store listing copy, which IS tracked.
store-listing/privacy-policy-gaps.md
store-listing/data-safety.md

# local integration-suite run artefacts (tests/integration)
tests/integration/.results/

# Private working docs / audit and eval reports — this repo is PUBLIC, never commit these.
# Keep them in docs-private/ (ignored); the explicit names guard against one landing in the root.
docs-private/
quality-eval*
secrets-audit.md
model-inventory.md
test-run-report.md
work-plan.md
verification-report.md
implementation-report.md
